IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `sda-vehicles`

-- Stamp Duty Act 1978 (NT) -- cases for the motor vehicle core (sda-vehicles.l4).
--
-- Expected values worked by hand from Schedule 1 cl 5 ("$3 for every $100 or fractional part of $100"), s 59 and
-- s 92A of the deposited reprint REPS013, never copied from the encoding's output. Clock for the regulative rules: days.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Stamp Duty Act 1978; see SOURCE-LICENSE.md.

§ `Cases -- the applicant registering a motor vehicle`

GIVEN `day`                  IS A DATE
      `at arm's length`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `price`                IS A NUMBER
      `delivery`             IS A NUMBER
      `value when agreed`    IS A NUMBER
      `value when applied`   IS A NUMBER
      `electric`             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Vehicle registration`
`a registration` MEANS
    `Vehicle registration` WITH
        `the date the certificate is issued`                                               IS `day`
        `it is a transfer by a sale and purchase at arm's length`                          IS `at arm's length`
        `the amount for which the vehicle and its additional equipment was sold`           IS `price`
        `the dealer delivery charges paid`                                                 IS `delivery`
        `the market value with additional equipment when the transaction was entered into` IS `value when agreed`
        `the market value with additional equipment when the application is made`          IS `value when applied`
        `it is an electric motor vehicle`                                                  IS `electric`

GIVEN `last registered to me`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `a bus never dutied`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `family gift`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `estate`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `wheelchair`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `trailer`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `tonnes`                 IS A NUMBER
      `veteran`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `non-commercial`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Vehicle exemption facts`
`exemption facts` MEANS
    `Vehicle exemption facts` WITH
        `it is issued to the person in whose name the vehicle was last registered`                           IS `last registered to me`
        `it seats 12 or more and the applicant has never paid stamp duty on it`                             IS `a bus never dutied`
        `it follows a gift to the spouse, parent, child or stepchild of the last registered owner, or jointly with them` IS `family gift`
        `it is issued to the executor, administrator or a beneficiary of a deceased estate, for the estate`  IS `estate`
        `the vehicle is a motorised wheelchair`                                                             IS `wheelchair`
        `the vehicle is a trailer or caravan`                                                               IS `trailer`
        `the trailer's gross vehicle mass, in tonnes`                                                       IS `tonnes`
        `it is issued to a veteran eligible for a pension at the VEA s 22(4) or 24(4) rate`                 IS `veteran`
        `the vehicle is for the veteran's non-commercial use`                                               IS `non-commercial`

`no exemption` MEANS `exemption facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE

§§ `s 59 and Schedule 1 cl 5 -- dutiable value and duty`

-- A used car bought from a dealer for $30 000 (deposit and trade-in included) plus $1 500 dealer delivery: $31 500;
-- 315 hundreds at $3 = $945.
#ASSERT `the dutiable value of the vehicle` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE 30000 1500 0 0 FALSE) EQUALS 31500
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the certificate of registration` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE 30000 1500 0 0 FALSE) `no exemption` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 945
-- $31 550: the part of $100 counts as a whole -- 316 hundreds, $948.
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 5 duty on` 31550 EQUALS 948
-- Not at arm's length: the greater of the market values, $20 000 when agreed and $19 500 when applied: $600.
#ASSERT `the dutiable value of the vehicle` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 12000 0 20000 19500 FALSE) EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the certificate of registration` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 12000 0 20000 19500 FALSE) `no exemption` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 600
-- Before 1 July 2017 the scale is not the deposited one.
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the certificate of registration` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2017 6 30) TRUE 30000 1500 0 0 FALSE) `no exemption` EQUALS `not covered` `the conveyance or registration is dated before 1 July 2017, when Schedule 1 was last amended (No. 13, 2017); the scale in force before then is not in the deposited reprint`

§§ `s 92A -- electric vehicles`

-- $60 000 electric car issued 1 March 2026: $1 800 less the duty on the first $50 000 ($1 500) = $300.
#ASSERT `the s 92A exemption` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE 60000 0 0 0 TRUE) EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the certificate of registration` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE 60000 0 0 0 TRUE) `no exemption` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 300
-- $40 000: all $1 200 exempt.
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the certificate of registration` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE 40000 0 0 0 TRUE) `no exemption` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
-- $50 001: duty $1 503, of which $1 500 is exempt -- the $1 500 cap (s 92A(4)) equals the duty on $50 000.
#ASSERT `the s 92A exemption` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE 50001 0 0 0 TRUE) EQUALS 1500
-- The window: 1 July 2022 to 30 June 2027.
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the certificate of registration` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) TRUE 60000 0 0 0 TRUE) `no exemption` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 1800
#ASSERT `the s 92A exemption` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2022 6 30) TRUE 60000 0 0 0 TRUE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the s 92A exemption` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2027 6 30) TRUE 60000 0 0 0 TRUE) EQUALS 1500
-- s 92A(3): no s 61 declaration for the concession; one for an item 23 exemption.
#ASSERT NOT (`a declaration of the grounds must be lodged with the application (s 61)` `the s 92A electric vehicle concession`)
#ASSERT `a declaration of the grounds must be lodged with the application (s 61)` `an item 23 exemption`

§§ `Schedule 2 item 23 -- exemptions`

-- (a) moving to the Territory with your own car: registered again in your name.
#ASSERT `the item 23 exemption for` (`exemption facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `exempt: re-registration in the name of the person it was last registered to (item 23(a))`
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the certificate of registration` (`a registration` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 0 0 30000 30000 FALSE) (`exemption facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
-- (a)(ii): not for a 12-seater on which the applicant never paid duty.
#ASSERT `the item 23 exemption for` (`exemption facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not exempt under the items encoded`
-- (b) a gift from a parent; (e) a deceased estate; (j)(i) a motorised wheelchair.
#ASSERT `the item 23 exemption for` (`exemption facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `exempt: a gift within the family (item 23(b))`
#ASSERT `the item 23 exemption for` (`exemption facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `exempt: a deceased estate (item 23(e))`
#ASSERT `the item 23 exemption for` (`exemption facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `exempt: a motorised wheelchair (item 23(j)(i))`
-- (j)(v) a caravan of 4.5 t is exempt; of 4.6 t it is not.
#ASSERT `the item 23 exemption for` (`exemption facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 4.5 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `exempt: a trailer of not more than 4.5 t (item 23(j)(v))`
#ASSERT `the item 23 exemption for` (`exemption facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 4.6 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not exempt under the items encoded`
-- (k) a veteran at the VEA s 24(4) rate, for private use; not for commercial use.
#ASSERT `the item 23 exemption for` (`exemption facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `exempt: a veteran at the special or extreme disablement rate, non-commercial use (item 23(k))`
#ASSERT NOT (`the certificate is exempt under item 23` (`exemption facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE))

§§ `ss 57, 59(3) and 59A -- regulative rules`

-- s 57(1): paid on the day the certificate issues.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 57(1) -- pay the duty to the Registrar before the certificate is issued` TRUE 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant for registration` `pay the Registrar the duty on the certificate` 0)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- An exempt certificate is not "liable to duty": nothing to pay.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 57(1) -- pay the duty to the Registrar before the certificate is issued` FALSE 0) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant for registration, "s 57(1): ..." (the certificate was to issue on day 3; paid day 4)
#TRACE `s 57(1) -- pay the duty to the Registrar before the certificate is issued` TRUE 3 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant for registration` DOES `pay the Registrar the duty on the certificate` AT 4
-- s 59(3): the seller notifies on day 14: in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 59(3) -- the transferor must notify the consideration within 14 days after the transfer` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the transferor of the vehicle` `notify the amount received as consideration for the transfer` 14)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `the days for the transferor to notify the consideration` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty under ss 57(1) and 59(5), in penalty units` EQUALS 50
-- expect: BREACH BY the transferor of the vehicle, "s 59(3), (5): ..." (notified on day 15)
#TRACE `s 59(3) -- the transferor must notify the consideration within 14 days after the transfer` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the transferor of the vehicle` DOES `notify the amount received as consideration for the transfer` AT 15
-- s 59A: the sale is undone in full: the duty must be refunded; not if the car was kept.
#ASSERT `the vehicle duty must be refunded under s 59A` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the vehicle duty must be refunded under s 59A` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 59A -- the Commissioner must refund the vehicle duty when the sale is undone` TRUE TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Commissioner` `refund the duty paid` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
